From 8a3892da2910379632ae264bf3929ed1238dacbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:41:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: cpr3: Add SDM660 CPRh support in open-loop mode

Add the SDM660 KBSS CPRh controllers, one per CPU cluster, with the
values of the vendor CPRh driver and device tree:

- Fuse reference voltages, open-loop fuse adjustments, RO scaling factors,
  sensor counts (6 power, 9 performance) and controller timings, with the
  1760 ns settling time and 1042 ns corner switch delay converted to
  register counts at 19.2 MHz (33 and 5).
- The speed bin 1 corner plan of both clusters, with the vendor per-corner
  floor, ceiling and floor-to-ceiling range voltages. The open-loop,
  floor and ceiling voltage of each corner are computed as the vendor
  driver does: the fused voltages are interpolated by frequency before
  rounding to the 4 mV step, limited to the corner floor and ceiling,
  kept clear of the 872 mV APM threshold (20 mV hysteresis), used as the
  corner ceiling, and the floor is raised to the ceiling minus the range.
  The common CPR3 code rounds each fuse voltage first, which gives up to
  4 mV more on some interpolated corners.
- Closed-loop operation stays off: the hardware closed loop is disabled
  and every corner has CL_DISABLE set, so the CPRh applies the open-loop
  voltage of the corner OSM selects. The closed-loop fuse adjustments are
  kept for the target quotients.
- The vendor RESET_STEP_QUOT_LOOP_EN bit and fixed step quotient field.
- The corner and control registers stay at 0x3a00 and 0x3aa0 as in the
  vendor driver, whatever the hardware revision reads.

Only speed bin 1 with CPR fusing revision 2 is supported. On any other
part the driver refuses to probe before touching the hardware, so the
CPU clocks and voltages stay as the bootloader set them.

The computed corner table is logged at probe. Also fix an out-of-bounds
read of the frequency ordering check at the first corner, check the
reference clock enable, and name the threads in the log messages.

Scope: SDM630/660 common
Porting notes: Local addition to the CPR3 driver (not upstream). Values from the vendor crDroid 4.19 tree: drivers/regulator/cprh-kbss-regulator.c and arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/sdm660-regulator.dtsi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
